---
description: Jira-to-PR conductor via shared CLI. Use when the user says dev-loop, /dev-loop, or work this Jira story.
alwaysApply: false
---

Cursor agent is the conductor. CLI is a **stepper** — never a 24h wait.

```bash
python3 ~/.claude/hooks/dev-loop/cli.py start KEY --repo PATH
python3 ~/.claude/hooks/dev-loop/cli.py step KEY
```

`continue` with `runtime.agent: cursor` is an alias of `step`. Do not use `continue --no-wait` (that runs every remaining stage with no agent).

Handshake under `~/.config/dev-conductor/dev-loop/runs/KEY/`:

- `STAGE_DONE` / `SESSION_DONE` — this agent writes when the **stage** is done
- `SPEC_APPROVED` / `APPROVED` — only after the user confirms the spec (AskQuestion). Not auto.
- Then `cli.py step KEY` again

Test-writer: spawn a **new Agent** whose prompt is only `spec.md` + `contracts.md`. Do not Read `src/main` in the parent chat. `beforeReadFile` also denies impl reads while `state.stage` is `test-writer`.

sessionStart lists open Jira keys when cwd is under `dev_root`.

Config: `~/.config/dev-conductor/dev-loop/config.yaml` (`runtime.agent: cursor`). Secrets: `~/.config/dev-conductor/secrets.env`. No Jira/GitHub MCP.
